---
/**
 * /deck — the three-slide outreach deck, live on the site itself.
 *
 * WHY THIS PAGE EXISTS. The deck was originally built as a standalone,
 * fully self-contained HTML file (fonts and the screenshot base64-embedded)
 * so it could be attached to an email with zero dependencies. This page is
 * the second, better home for it: a real URL on the actual deployed site,
 * so it can be LINKED instead of attached — the deliverability notes in
 * outreach/notes.md specifically recommend not attaching the PDF to a cold
 * first email, and a link here is the natural alternative for a follow-up.
 *
 * WHY IT DOESN'T USE BaseLayout. Every other page on this site is a fluid,
 * responsive marketing page with a nav, a footer, a sticky call bar and the
 * concept badge. A slide deck is a different kind of object — three fixed
 * 16:9 frames meant to read identically on screen and on paper. Forcing it
 * through the same chrome as a homepage would fight that. So this page
 * writes its own <html>, but still imports the SAME tokens.css, the SAME
 * two fonts, and the SAME SEOHead component everything else uses — nothing
 * here is a second copy of the brand, it is the first copy, reused.
 *
 * WHY NO CONCEPT BADGE. The badge exists to stop a page that SIMULATES
 * their real website from being mistaken for it (CLAUDE.md §11). This page
 * doesn't simulate anything — slide 1 states in its own copy, in the open,
 * that it's "a concept redesign for Approved Contractor, Inc., built
 * specifically for them, unprompted." That is the same disclosure the badge
 * makes, just written as a sentence instead of a floating pill, which fits
 * a pitch deck better than a live-site mockup. It's still not indexable —
 * see the SEOHead call below, and the site-wide robots.txt Disallow: /
 * already covers this path too.
 *
 * CONTENT PARITY. The copy and layout here are the same three slides
 * already verified against WCAG AA and print-tested as a PDF in
 * outreach/deck/index.html. That file remains the canonical source for the
 * PDF attachment sent in a warm follow-up; this page is the linkable web
 * version of the same three slides. If one changes, change both.
 */
import "@fontsource-variable/source-serif-4/wght.css";
import "@fontsource-variable/outfit/wght.css";
import "../styles/tokens.css";

import { getImage } from "astro:assets";
import SEOHead from "../components/core/SEOHead.astro";
import StampMark from "../components/core/StampMark.astro";
import deckHeroSrc from "../assets/deck/deck-hero.jpg";
import { SITE } from "../config/site";

// A plain optimized <img>, not <Image>/<Picture> — this page is a fixed
// 1280px print-style layout, not the fluid responsive system the rest of
// the site uses, so the automatic responsive-layout CSS those components
// inject would fight the slide's fixed sizing rather than help it.
const deckHero = await getImage({
  src: deckHeroSrc,
  width: 1200,
  format: "webp",
  quality: 82,
});
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <SEOHead
      title="The concept, in three slides"
      description={`A three-slide look at the concept redesign built for ${SITE.legalName}: what it is, why it matters, and what it costs.`}
      path="/deck"
    />
    <style>
      /* ==================================================================
         Everything below reads var(--n-*), var(--b-*), var(--face-*), etc.
         DIRECTLY from tokens.css, imported above. No values are re-declared
         here — this is what "styled from the project's own tokens.css" means
         literally, not by resemblance.
         ================================================================== */
      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      html, body {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        background: #d8d3d0;
        font-family: var(--face-body);
        color: var(--n-800);
      }

      .deck-back {
        position: fixed;
        top: 14px;
        left: 14px;
        z-index: 10;
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        min-height: 2.75rem;
        padding: 0 14px;
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: var(--n-900);
        color: #fff;
        font-size: 13px;
        font-weight: 600;
        text-decoration: none;
        box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.22);
      }
      .deck-back:hover { background: var(--b-600); }
      .deck-back:focus-visible {
        outline: 3px solid var(--b-600);
        outline-offset: 2px;
      }

      .slide {
        position: relative;
        width: 1280px;
        height: 720px;
        margin: 24px auto;
        overflow: hidden;
        background: var(--n-000);
        box-shadow: 0 10px 40px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.18);
        page-break-after: always;
        break-after: page;
      }
      .slide:last-of-type { page-break-after: auto; break-after: auto; }

      /* Screen-only: clears the fixed "back to site" pill above slide 1.
         MUST stay scoped to screen — .slide:first-of-type has higher
         specificity than the plain .slide selector in the print reset
         below, so an unscoped margin-top here would win over `margin: 0`
         in print and push the whole deck 72px past the 720px @page height,
         silently producing a 4th, mostly-blank page. Caught by rendering
         the actual PDF and counting pages: 4 instead of 3. */
      @media screen {
        .slide:first-of-type { margin-top: 72px; }
      }

      @media screen and (max-width: 1320px) {
        .slide { width: 100vw; }
      }

      @page { size: 1280px 720px; margin: 0; }
      @media print {
        html, body { background: #fff; }
        .slide { margin: 0; box-shadow: none; }
        .no-print { display: none !important; }
      }

      .eyebrow {
        font-family: var(--face-body);
        font-size: 13px;
        font-weight: 600;
        letter-spacing: 0.14em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
      }

      /* ---- Slide 1 — What this is --------------------------------------- */
      .s1 { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
      .s1__band {
        background-image: var(--grad-brand);
        background-color: var(--b-600);
        padding: 18px 56px 15px;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: space-between;
      }
      .s1__band-note {
        text-align: right;
        font-size: 13px;
        line-height: 1.4;
        color: var(--b-100);
        max-width: 260px;
      }
      .s1__band-note strong { color: #fff; font-weight: 600; }

      .s1__body {
        flex: 1;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        gap: 13px;
        padding: 14px 56px 12px;
        text-align: center;
      }
      .s1__headline {
        font-family: var(--face-display);
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 30px;
        line-height: 1.18;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
        color: var(--n-900);
        max-width: 900px;
        margin: 0;
      }
      .s1__headline em {
        font-style: normal;
        color: var(--b-600);
      }
      .s1__shot {
        width: 740px;
        max-width: 80%;
        margin: 0;
        border-radius: var(--radius-card);
        overflow: hidden;
        box-shadow: var(--shadow-l);
        border: 1px solid var(--n-200);
      }
      .s1__shot img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
      .s1__idea {
        max-width: 780px;
        font-size: 15.5px;
        line-height: 1.55;
        color: var(--n-600);
        margin: 0;
      }
      .s1__idea strong { color: var(--n-900); font-weight: 600; }

      /* ---- Slide 2 — Why it matters -------------------------------------- */
      .s2 { display: flex; flex-direction: column; height: 100%; padding: 48px 64px 40px; }
      .s2__eyebrow { color: var(--b-600); margin-bottom: 10px; }
      .s2__heading {
        font-family: var(--face-display);
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 32px;
        line-height: 1.16;
        letter-spacing: -0.012em;
        color: var(--n-900);
        max-width: 780px;
        margin: 0 0 8px;
      }
      .s2__sub { font-size: 15px; color: var(--n-600); max-width: 640px; margin: 0 0 30px; }
      .s2__points {
        flex: 1;
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
        gap: 28px;
      }
      @media screen and (max-width: 900px) {
        .s2__points { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      }
      .s2__point {
        background: var(--color-surface);
        border: 1px solid var(--n-200);
        border-radius: var(--radius-card);
        padding: 26px 24px 22px;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 12px;
      }
      .s2__num {
        font-family: var(--face-display);
        font-weight: 900;
        font-size: 15px;
        color: var(--b-600);
        letter-spacing: 0.02em;
      }
      .s2__point h3 {
        font-family: var(--face-display);
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 19px;
        line-height: 1.28;
        color: var(--n-900);
        margin: 0;
      }
      .s2__point p { font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--n-800); margin: 0; }
      .s2__point .src {
        margin-top: auto;
        padding-top: 10px;
        font-size: 12px;
        font-style: italic;
        color: var(--a-700);
      }

      /* ---- Slide 3 — What it costs ---------------------------------------- */
      .s3 { display: flex; flex-direction: column; height: 100%; padding: 40px 64px 26px; }
      .s3__eyebrow { color: var(--b-600); margin-bottom: 8px; }
      .s3__heading {
        font-family: var(--face-display);
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 28px;
        line-height: 1.15;
        color: var(--n-900);
        margin: 0 0 18px;
      }
      .s3__primary {
        background-image: var(--grad-brand);
        background-color: var(--b-600);
        border-radius: var(--radius-card);
        color: #fff;
        padding: 20px 28px;
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
        gap: 24px;
        align-items: center;
        margin-bottom: 14px;
      }
      @media screen and (max-width: 900px) {
        .s3__primary { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      }
      .s3__price { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 14px; white-space: nowrap; }
      .s3__price-old {
        font-family: var(--face-body);
        font-size: 22px;
        font-weight: 500;
        color: var(--b-100);
        text-decoration: line-through;
        text-decoration-thickness: 2.5px;
        text-decoration-color: #fff;
      }
      .s3__price-new {
        font-family: var(--face-display);
        font-weight: 900;
        font-size: 52px;
        line-height: 1;
        color: #fff;
      }
      .s3__primary-copy h3 {
        margin: 0 0 6px;
        font-family: var(--face-display);
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 18px;
      }
      .s3__primary-list {
        margin: 0 0 8px;
        padding: 0;
        list-style: none;
        font-size: 13px;
        line-height: 1.7;
        color: #fff;
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 4px 0;
      }
      .s3__primary-list li { white-space: nowrap; }
      .s3__primary-list li:not(:last-child)::after {
        content: "·";
        margin: 0 10px;
        color: var(--b-100);
      }
      .s3__reason { margin: 0; font-size: 13px; font-style: italic; color: var(--b-100); }

      .s3__row {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.3fr;
        gap: 14px;
        margin-bottom: 12px;
        flex: 1;
        min-height: 0;
      }
      @media screen and (max-width: 900px) {
        .s3__row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      }
      .s3__card {
        background: var(--color-surface);
        border: 1px solid var(--n-200);
        border-radius: var(--radius-card);
        padding: 16px 20px;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
      }
      .s3__card h4 {
        margin: 0 0 4px;
        font-family: var(--face-display);
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 15px;
        color: var(--n-900);
      }
      .s3__card .tag {
        display: inline-block;
        font-size: 11px;
        font-weight: 600;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--b-600);
        margin-bottom: 6px;
      }
      .s3__card .price {
        font-family: var(--face-display);
        font-weight: 900;
        font-size: 22px;
        color: var(--n-900);
        margin: 0 0 6px;
      }
      .s3__card p { margin: 0; font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--n-800); }
      .s3__card .fine { margin-top: 8px; font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--n-600); }
      .s3__card .fine b { color: var(--n-800); font-weight: 600; }

      .s3__care-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 8px 16px; margin-top: 8px; }
      .s3__care-grid div { font-size: 11.5px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--n-800); }
      .s3__care-grid .lbl {
        font-size: 10.5px;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.05em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--n-600);
        margin-bottom: 2px;
      }

      .s3__foot {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 20px;
        background: var(--n-050);
        border: 1px solid var(--n-200);
        border-radius: var(--radius-card);
        padding: 12px 20px;
      }
      .s3__foot-marketing { font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--n-800); max-width: 62%; margin: 0; }
      .s3__foot-marketing b { color: var(--n-900); }
      .s3__foot-why {
        font-size: 12px;
        font-style: italic;
        line-height: 1.5;
        color: var(--n-600);
        max-width: 34%;
        text-align: right;
        margin: 0;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="no-print deck-back" href="/">← Back to the concept site</a>

    <!-- ================= SLIDE 1 — What this is ================= -->
    <section class="slide s1">
      <div class="s1__band on-brand">
        <StampMark size="lg" />
        <div class="s1__band-note">
          A concept redesign for <strong>{SITE.legalName}</strong>, built
          specifically for them, unprompted.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="s1__body">
        <h1 class="s1__headline">
          Same business. Same license. <em>A site that actually shows it.</em>
        </h1>

        <figure class="s1__shot">
          <img
            src={deckHero.src}
            width={deckHero.attributes.width}
            height={deckHero.attributes.height}
            alt="The concept homepage for Approved Contractor, Inc., built around their own scarlet stamp mark and their real California contractor license."
          />
        </figure>

        <p class="s1__idea">
          <strong>The idea is simple:</strong> the company is called Approved
          Contractor. The whole site is built around that one word, backed
          up. Their real license, current and checkable, is right at the top
          instead of buried in a footer, set in their own red and their own
          stamp mark instead of a stock template.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ================= SLIDE 2 — Why it matters ================= -->
    <section class="slide s2">
      <p class="eyebrow s2__eyebrow">Why it matters</p>
      <h2 class="s2__heading">What a working site actually does for a business like this.</h2>
      <p class="s2__sub">Not features. What a homeowner actually experiences in the first ten seconds.</p>

      <div class="s2__points">
        <div class="s2__point">
          <span class="s2__num">01</span>
          <h3>Someone can check you're real.</h3>
          <p>
            A homeowner comparing three quotes can verify the license is
            active without taking anyone's word for it. It's on the page,
            dated, with a link straight to the state lookup.
          </p>
          <span class="src">Verified against the CSLB register, license #952272</span>
        </div>
        <div class="s2__point">
          <span class="s2__num">02</span>
          <h3>Your own reviews do the talking.</h3>
          <p>
            Customers already thank Jared by name, unprompted, in their
            reviews. That's what a new visitor reads first now, not a stock
            photo of someone else's living room.
          </p>
          <span class="src">From reviews already published, quoted verbatim</span>
        </div>
        <div class="s2__point">
          <span class="s2__num">03</span>
          <h3>The call button works on a phone.</h3>
          <p>
            Most people find a contractor while searching on their phone.
            The button they'd tap to call should not be sitting behind a
            chat popup the second the page loads.
          </p>
          <span class="src">Seen on the current site today, mobile view</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ================= SLIDE 3 — What it costs ================= -->
    <section class="slide s3">
      <p class="eyebrow s3__eyebrow">What it costs</p>
      <h2 class="s3__heading">Three ways to take this further, and one honest reason for the price.</h2>

      <div class="s3__primary on-brand">
        <div class="s3__price">
          <span class="s3__price-old">$2,450</span>
          <span class="s3__price-new">$700</span>
        </div>
        <div class="s3__primary-copy">
          <h3>1 · Take it as is</h3>
          <ul class="s3__primary-list">
            <li>Your content and photos swapped in</li>
            <li>Minor changes to fit your business</li>
            <li>SEO set up properly</li>
            <li>Live on your own domain</li>
            <li>Everything handed over, you own all of it</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="s3__reason">
            Why it's less: the site's already built. I'm not starting from
            a blank page, so I'm not pricing it like one.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="s3__row">
        <div class="s3__card">
          <span class="tag">2 · Custom</span>
          <p class="price">From $1,500</p>
          <h4>Take it further</h4>
          <p>More pages, deeper customization, built around how you actually run things day to day.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="s3__card">
          <span class="tag">3 · Ongoing</span>
          <p class="price">
            $99<span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:500;color:var(--n-600)">/mo</span>
            &nbsp;or&nbsp;<span style="color:var(--n-900)">$69/mo</span> billed annually
          </p>
          <h4>Let me look after it</h4>
          <div class="s3__care-grid">
            <div>
              <div class="lbl">Included, within reason</div>
              Hosting and technical upkeep, keeping SEO healthy, text and
              copy edits, swapping photos, updating hours, prices, menus or
              services, and seasonal changes.
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="lbl">Quoted separately, à la carte</div>
              New pages or sections, branding or logo work, photography, new
              long-form content, new features, and anything that's a new
              project rather than an update.
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="fine">
            <b>"Within reason" is used plainly, not as an escape hatch:</b>
            it means small updates and maintenance. Anything bigger is
            quoted before any work starts, so there's never a surprise
            invoice. That boundary is also what keeps the monthly this low.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="s3__foot">
        <p class="s3__foot-marketing">
          <b>4 · Marketing support</b> — scope to be discussed. On top of
          the build, hands-on help from a brand-first marketing executive:
          13+ years at CMO level building brands that have generated
          billions of earned impressions and communities of millions.
        </p>
        <p class="s3__foot-why">
          Nobody hired me for any of this. I did it because I like the
          work, and I'd rather start a relationship than win a bidding war.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </body>
</html>
